uangdong Key Laboratory of Intelligent Information Processing, Shenzhen University, China."}]}}, {"fullName": "Hering A", "lastName": "Hering", "firstName": "Alessa", "initials": "A", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7602-803X"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Fraunhofer Institute for Digital Medicine MEVIS, Lübeck, Germany."}]}}, {"fullName": "Vilaça JL", "lastName": "Vilaça", "firstName": "João L", "initials": "JL", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-4196-5357"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "2Ai - School of Technology, IPCA, Barcelos, Portugal."}]}}, {"fullName": "Flores M", "lastName": "Flores", "firstName": "Mona", "initials": "M", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "NVIDIA, Bethesda, MD, USA; Santa Clara, CA, USA; Munich, Germany."}]}}, {"fullName": "Xu D", "lastName": "Xu", "firstName": "Daguang", "initials": "D", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "NVIDIA, Bethesda, MD, USA; Santa Clara, CA, USA; Munich, Germany."}]}}, {"fullName": "Wood B", "lastName": "Wood", "firstName": "Bradford", "initials": "B", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-4297-0051"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Radiology and Imaging Sciences, National Institutes of Health Clinical Center, Bethesda, MD, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Linguraru MG", "lastName": "Linguraru", "firstName": "Marius George", "initials": "MG", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Sheikh Zayed Institute for Pediatric Surgical Innovation, Children's National Hospital, WA, DC, USA; School of Medicine and Health Sciences, George Washington University, WA, DC, USA."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9404-5127"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3662-8743"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-4196-5357"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-4297-0051"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5216-3528"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5728-6869"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6626-2463"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7602-803X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-8154-5875"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1616-2234"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0005-7407-893X"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"volume": "82", "journalIssueId": 3443640, "dateOfPublication": "2022 Nov", "monthOfPublication": 11, "yearOfPublication": 2022, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Med Image Anal", "title": "Medical image analysis", "essn": "1361-8423", "issn": "1361-8415", "nlmid": "9713490", "isoabbreviation": "Med Image Anal"}, "printPublicationDate": "2022-11-01"}, "pubYear": "2022", "pageInfo": "102605", "abstractText": "Artificial intelligence (AI) methods for the automatic detection and quantification of COVID-19 lesions in chest computed tomography (CT) might play an important role in the monitoring and management of the disease. We organized an international challenge and competition for the development and comparison of AI algorithms for this task, which we supported with public data and state-of-the-art benchmark methods. Board Certified Radiologists annotated 295 public images from two sources (A and B) for algorithms training (n=199, source A), validation (n=50, source A) and testing (n=23, source A; n=23, source B). There were 1,096 registered teams of which 225 and 98 completed the validation and testing phases, respectively. The challenge showed that AI models could be rapidly designed by diverse teams with the potential to measure disease or facilitate timely and patient-specific interventions. This paper provides an overview and the major outcomes of the COVID-19 Lung CT Lesion Segmentation Challenge - 2020.", "affiliation": "NVIDIA, Bethesda, MD, USA; Santa Clara, CA, USA